# Local development secrets for `pnpm dev:api`. Copy to `.dev.vars`, which is gitignored.
#
#   cp apps/api/.dev.vars.example apps/api/.dev.vars
#
# These are NOT the production values and must never be. Production secrets are set with
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` and never pass through this file, the repository, or CI
# (docs/OPERATIONS.md § Secrets).
#
# Without them, `GET /v1/challenge` fails: an empty HMAC key is rejected by WebCrypto, which
# is why the Worker now refuses the request up front with a log line naming the binding.

POW_SECRET="local-development-pow-secret-not-for-production"
IP_HASH_SECRET="local-development-ip-hash-secret-not-for-production"

# The Cloudflare credentials the provisioning saga needs. `POST /v1/tunnels` will refuse with a
# logged `INTERNAL` until all four are present, which is deliberate: a control plane that answers
# `/v1/meta` cheerfully while being unable to provision anything is the worst kind of half-working.
#
# The placeholders below are enough to *start* the Worker, not to provision: every Cloudflare call
# will be rejected upstream. Use a real scoped token (Account → Cloudflare Tunnel → Edit, Zone → DNS
# → Edit) against a zone you own if you need the lifecycle end to end, and never a production one.
CF_API_TOKEN="local-development-not-a-real-token"
CF_ACCOUNT_ID="0000000000000000000000000000000o"
CF_ZONE_ID="0000000000000000000000000000000o"
CF_DOMAIN="nport.test"

# Routes every Cloudflare call to the in-memory fake in src/cloudflare/dev-fake.ts, so
# `POST /v1/tunnels` succeeds without credentials and `pnpm dev` provisions offline. The lease, the
# saga, the ownerToken, the heartbeats and the URL are all real; the connector token is not, so the
# real edge refuses it at registration and the CLI retries, gives up, and releases the lease.
#
# This flag can only reach a Worker through this file, which `wrangler deploy` never uploads — and
# the fake refuses to activate anyway when CF_API_TOKEN looks like a real one, so putting a genuine
# token above silently gets you the genuine API. Set it to "" to always use the real thing.
FAKE_CLOUDFLARE="1"

# Lowers the client-version floor to match what the workspace actually builds.
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` sets it to 3.0.0 for production, and `crates/cli` is version 3.0.0-dev — which
# semver puts *below* 3.0.0, so the local CLI is refused by the local control plane with
# CLIENT_TOO_OLD. That ordering is deliberate and must not be "fixed" in the gate: it is what stops
# every 3.0.0-beta.N client sailing through the moment the floor moves to 3.0.0
# (`src/middleware/client-gate.ts`).
#
# 3.0.0-dev rather than 0.0.0 on purpose — the gate still runs and a real 2.x client is still
# refused, so what is being exercised locally is the production code path, not a disabled one.
# A `.dev.vars` entry overrides the matching `vars` value, and only under `wrangler dev`.
MIN_CLIENT_VERSION="3.0.0-dev"
